From ea77bbd1fb2675f1334b0f2d537aeb6346561a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Burke Cates <burke.cates@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:19:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM: soundwire: qcom: acknowledge interrupts before handling
 them

qcom_swrm_irq_handler() reads the interrupt status, runs the handlers,
then writes the same status value to the clear register. An event that
latches again while the handlers run is cleared with it and lost.

This happens with peripheral alerts: a status change to ALERT latches
both SLAVE_PEND_IRQ and CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS. The alert handler
services the peripherals' SCP_INT1, which takes them back to ATTACHED
and latches CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS again. If that happens after the
CHANGE_ENUM handler read SWRM_MCP_SLV_STATUS, the late clear drops the
new edge and the core keeps the peripheral in ALERT. On the ASUS Zenbook
A16 (two WSA8845 per bus) parity errors on s2idle resume hit both amps
of a bus at once, and one of them was left in "Alert" in 1 of ~3
resumes with parity, until the next status change.

Clear the latched bits first, so an event during handling is seen by
the status re-read at the end of the loop.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
Not-for-upstream: local workaround for one laptop, not reviewed for
  submission; use only for local testing.

 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index c2d6eb4abb5c..6b2d6231d53a 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -860,6 +860,15 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_swrm_irq_handler(int irq, void *dev_id)
 	intr_sts_masked = intr_sts & ctrl->intr_mask;
 
 	do {
+		/*
+		 * Acknowledge before handling. Servicing a peripheral alert
+		 * makes it go from ALERT back to ATTACHED, which latches
+		 * CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS again; when that bit was already
+		 * set in intr_sts, clearing it after the handlers lost the
+		 * new edge, and the peripheral stayed in ALERT.
+		 */
+		ctrl->reg_write(ctrl, ctrl->reg_layout[SWRM_REG_INTERRUPT_CLEAR],
+				intr_sts);
 		for (i = 0; i < SWRM_INTERRUPT_MAX; i++) {
 			value = intr_sts_masked & BIT(i);
 			if (!value)
@@ -987,8 +996,6 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_swrm_irq_handler(int irq, void *dev_id)
 				break;
 			}
 		}
-		ctrl->reg_write(ctrl, ctrl->reg_layout[SWRM_REG_INTERRUPT_CLEAR],
-				intr_sts);
 		ctrl->reg_read(ctrl, ctrl->reg_layout[SWRM_REG_INTERRUPT_STATUS],
 			       &intr_sts);
 		intr_sts_masked = intr_sts & ctrl->intr_mask;
